
README -- frequency analysis functions (helpers/)

Per-subject analysis
- run_freq_analysis_mean.m
  Per-subject FOOOF-based frequency analysis. For each condition, splits
  the PSD into periodic/aperiodic/total components, computes AUC per
  band + broadband, and the aperiodic exponent/offset. Saves one R
  struct per subject.
- fun_epoch_reject.m
  Drops bad epochs before spectral analysis (dependency of
  run_freq_analysis_mean).
- get_aux_freq.m
  Pulls in AUX-derived frequency info per subject (dependency of
  run_freq_analysis_mean).

Cluster-based stats (channel topographies)
- fun_plot_topos_T_stats.m
  Paired cluster-based permutation T-test (each condition vs baseline),
  one topography per comparison, FDR-corrected across comparisons.
  Returns report_txt plus Cohen's d effect sizes (max/mean within each
  significant cluster) and cluster p-values, each as a struct.
- fun_plot_topos_iv_regression.m
  Within-subject cluster-based regression of a topo measure against a
  continuous IV (e.g. ASC rating). One topography (the regression
  T-map). Returns report_txt plus a within-subject correlation (r) as
  effect size, and cluster p-values.
- fun_plot_topos_iv_regression_bands.m
  Same regression as above, run separately per frequency band, plotted
  together with a shared color scale and FDR correction across bands.

Modulation index (MI) plots
- plot_MI_single.m
  Plots one measure's modulation index vs baseline across conditions,
  with significance testing per condition.
- plot_MI_comparison.m
  Same idea but overlays periodic/aperiodic/total MI on one plot per
  band, plus a direct periodic-vs-aperiodic comparison. Returns
  report_txt plus the per-measure and direct-comparison stats as
  structs.

