README -- main frequency results script

Loads the per-subject R structs saved by run_freq_analysis_mean.m, builds
grand-average matrices, and produces the Figure 2 panels plus supporting
stats text files. Run top to bottom, section by section (each %% block
is independent once the load/merge section has run).

- Setup & load
  Loads FieldTrip, the canonical 63-channel layout (reset_elec_63.mat),
  and all *_freq.mat files into one R struct array. Assigns each subject
  a PID number and selects the breathwork (BW) sessions (PMR line is
  there too, commented out).

- Analysis scope
  Defines the 5 rated conditions (baseline + R1-R4), the 5 frequency
  bands (delta-gamma), and the condition/band color maps used
  throughout.

- ASC ratings
  Builds start/end/mean/z-scored ASC ratings per subject*condition, the
  within- and between-condition deltas, and tertile/low-high ASC
  categories (pooled cutpoints).

- QC
  Mean FOOOF r2 and epoch counts across all 7 recorded conditions, plus
  a repeated-measures ANOVA checking for a condition effect on epoch
  count.

- Build topo + grand-average matrices
  Per-channel, per-subject, per-condition matrices for broadband
  total/periodic/aperiodic AUC, exponent, offset, and the same AUC
  measures split by band.

- R2 dependency
  Correlates each power measure (total/periodic/aperiodic) against FOOOF
  fit quality (r2), per band, to check the measures aren't just tracking
  fit quality.

- PSD panel
  Raw PSD, fitted aperiodic line, and residual (oscillatory) power,
  averaged across subjects, one line per condition, shared y-axis across
  the first two panels.

- Modulation index plots
  Exponent MI (plot_MI_single), periodic/aperiodic/total MI overlaid for
  broadband and per-band (plot_MI_comparison). Each saves an .svg figure
  and a _stats.txt via report_txt.

- Cluster topographies (vs baseline)
  Paired cluster-based T-tests (fun_plot_topos_T_stats) for broadband
  total/periodic/aperiodic, exponent, and each measure split by band.
  Each saves a topoT_*.svg figure and a clusterstats_*.txt.

- ASC topo relationships (currently "not used")
  Within-subject cluster regression of exponent (single topo,
  fun_plot_topos_iv_regression) and total/aperiodic/periodic power
  (per-band, fun_plot_topos_iv_regression_bands) against the ASC rating.
  Each saves a regression_*.svg figure and a regression_*.txt.

